",\"halve-a\",\"halve-a\"]. fixed_point = True because after 4 sweeps no change.\n\nBut we must be careful: The description says \"Each pass performs at most its first eligible rewrite per sweep.\" That suggests that for each pass, if there are multiple occurrences of 'old', only the first is replaced. So our interpretation is correct.\n\nNow implement solve(case) that returns JSON object with keys: text, applications, fixed_point.\n\nWe must not mutate case. We'll extract fields: text, passes, max_rounds.\n\nSteps: \n- Initialize current = case[\"text\"]\n- applications = []\n- rounds = 0\n- changed = True\n- While changed and rounds < max_rounds:\n    changed = False\n    for p in passes:\n        old = p[\"old\"]\n        new = p[\"new\"]\n        # find first occurrence of old in current\n        idx = current.find(old)\n        if idx != -1:\n            # replace first occurrence\n            current = current[:idx] + new + current[idx+len(old):]\n            changed = True\n            applications.append(p[\"name\"])\n    rounds += 1\n- fixed_point = not changed  # if loop ended because no change\nBut note: If max_rounds reached and still changed, fixed_point should be False. So fixed_point = (not changed) or (rounds < max_rounds and not changed). Actually we break only when changed is False or rounds >= max_rounds. After loop, if changed is False => fixed_point True. If changed is True (because max_rounds reached) => fixed_point False.\n\nImplementation: after loop, fixed_point = not changed.\n\nEdge cases: empty passes? Probably not.\n\nReturn dict with {\"text\": current, \"applications\": applications, \"fixed_point\": fixed_point}.\n\nWe must validate every required field. The case object should have text (string), passes (list of objects with name, old, new), max_rounds (int). We can assume they are present per contract.\n\nNow produce the JSON output: {\"implementation\": \"the Python source code as a string\"}.\n\nWe need to escape newlines, backslashes, quotes. Use json.dumps to generate the string properly.\n\nWrite the code as a multi-line string, then use json.dumps to embed it.\n\nImplementation:\n\nimport json\n\ndef solve(case):\n    text = case[\"text\"]\n    passes = case[\"passes\"]\n    max_rounds = case[\"max_rounds\"]\n    current = text\n    applications = []\n    changed = True\n    rounds = 0\n    while changed and rounds < max_rounds:\n        changed = False\n        for p in passes:\n            old = p[\"old\"]\n            new = p[\"new\"]\n            idx = current.find(old)\n            if idx != -1:\n                current = current[:idx] + new + current[idx+len(old):]\n                changed = True\n                applications.append(p[\"name\"])\n        rounds += 1\n    fixed_point = not changed\n    return {\"text\": current, \"applications\": applications, \"fixed_point\": fixed_point}\n\nThen produce output envelope:\n\n{\n  \"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    text = case[\\\"text\\\"]\\n    passes = case[\\\"passes\\\"]\\n    max_rounds = case[\\\"max_rounds\\\"]\\n    current = text\\n    applications = []\\n    changed = True\\n    rounds = 0\\n    while changed and rounds < max_rounds:\\n        changed = False\\n        for p in passes:\\n            old = p[\\\"old\\\"]\\n            new = p[\\\"new\\\"]\\n            idx = current.find(old)\\n            if idx != -1:\\n                current = current[:idx] + new + current[idx+len(old):]\\n                changed = True\\n                applications.append(p[\\\"name\\\"])\\n        rounds += 1\\n    fixed_point = not changed\\n    return {\\\"text\\\": current, \\\"applications\\\": applications, \\\"fixed_point\\\": fixed_point}\\n\"\n}\n\nBut we must ensure the source is a proper string. Use json.dumps to escape.\n\nLet's produce the final answer."},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":1195,"completion_tokens":1905,"total_tokens":3100,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":115